load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A Petri net: a model of concurrent processes, a bipartite graph of places (holding tokens) and transitions (firing
# when their input places are filled, moving tokens), capturing parallelism, synchronization, and resource flow without
# a global clock. It is the natural model for distributed and asynchronous computation. The form carries the set of
# places; the transitions and the token marking are the dynamics.
form petri-net
  link places, like set
